xen-mapcache: Fix invalidate performance

If there are many simultaneous invalidate calls via coroutines, the invalidate
call will be scheduled in a bh function. However, these bh functions will only
be executed during the next iteration of aio_bh_poll() and in reverse order of
submission. I observed up to 100 ms delay for some invalidate operations when
installing Windows Server 2025 with 64 vCPUs. This is long enough to cause the
installation to fail.

Fix the delays and installation failure by maintaining a queue of invalidations
(so that they are executed in order) and executing multiple invalidations in
one go.

Signed-off-by: Ross Lagerwall <ross.lagerwall@citrix.com>
